          "node_name": "Video 01 - Chủ đề: Đừng trách bản thân",
          "node_type": "generate",
          "provider": null,
          "prompt": "Create a 10-second vertical animated video, aspect ratio 9:16, based on the provided storyboard image.\n\nIMPORTANT REQUIREMENTS:\nThis video MUST include Vietnamese voice-over narration.\nThe voice-over MUST be a deep, calm Vietnamese male voice.\nThis video MUST include Vietnamese subtitles.\nThe voice-over and subtitles must be perfectly synchronized with each scene.\nDo not create a silent video.\nDo not skip the voice-over.\nDo not change the order of the storyboard frames.\n\nVERY IMPORTANT VISUAL RULE:\nDo NOT show the full storyboard sheet in the video.\nDo NOT show multiple storyboard frames in one video frame.\nEach storyboard frame must become a separate full-screen scene.\nThe final video must play scene by scene, one frame at a time, as individual cinematic shots.\nCrop or expand each storyboard frame to fill the 9:16 screen.\nNo contact sheet layout, no panel grid, no multiple frames visible at once.\n\nUse the storyboard frames in this exact order:\nFRAME 01 — 0s–2.5s\nFRAME 02 — 2.5s–5s\nFRAME 03 — 5s–7.5s\nFRAME 04 — 7.5s–10s\n\nVisual style:\nMinimalist hand-drawn cartoon stickman style, tiny stickman child, muted navy blue background, thick uneven black outlines, cinematic side lighting, soft shadows, lonely but healing atmosphere, emotional visual metaphor, simple composition.\n\nScene animation:\nFRAME 01 — 0s–2.5s:\nShow only this frame as a full-screen scene. A tiny stickman child stands alone in deep shadows, head slightly lowered, surrounded by empty space.\nVoice-over and subtitle:\n“Đừng trách bản thân mình.”\n\nFRAME 02 — 2.5s–5s:\nShow only this frame as a full-screen scene. The child slowly looks up while blurred adult stickman silhouettes walk past without noticing.\nVoice-over and subtitle:\n“Không phải ai cũng để tâm đến bạn.”\n\nFRAME 03 — 5s–7.5s:\nShow only this frame as a full-screen scene. Floating thought bubbles appear around the child, showing different people busy in their own worlds.\nVoice-over and subtitle:\n“Đừng mong người khác hiểu hết lòng mình.”\n\nFRAME 04 — 7.5s–10s:\nShow only this frame as a full-screen scene. Many adult stickman figures are enclosed in their own transparent bubbles, while the child quietly watches from the shadows.\nVoice-over and subtitle:\n“Ai cũng đang bận với cuộc đời của họ.”\n\nVoice-over direction:\nDeep Vietnamese male voice, calm, warm, slow, emotional, reflective, healing tone, natural spoken rhythm. The narration must be audible from beginning to end.\n\nSubtitle direction:\nVietnamese subtitles at the bottom center of the screen.\nUse clear white text with subtle dark shadow for readability.\nEach subtitle must appear exactly when the matching voice-over line is spoken.\nDo not display all subtitles at once.\nDo not add extra text.\n\nMotion direction:\nSlow push-in camera, subtle breathing motion, gentle shadow flicker, slow walking silhouettes, drifting thought bubbles.\nKeep animation minimal, poetic, cinematic, and emotionally soft.\n\nFinal requirement:\nThe final output must be a complete video with separate full-screen scenes, synchronized Vietnamese deep male voice-over, and matching Vietnamese subtitles. No silent version. No storyboard grid visible in the video.",
