          "prompt": "Use the attached reference images as the visual style guide.\n\nCOMMON STYLE CONSTRAINTS — apply to all frames:\nCreate a vertical panel storyboard illustration arranged like a cinematic contact sheet. Use a stylized hand-drawn comic / anime illustration style based on the references: a muscular masked humanoid character with a metallic golden-yellow body, black mask with sharp white eyes, bold black outlines, cel-shaded rendering, dark charcoal / muted navy background, minimal environment, strong silhouette design, dramatic side lighting, soft shadows, and a moody emotional atmosphere. Keep the visual language minimal but powerful, with clean composition, clear storytelling, and consistent character design across all frames. The overall look should feel cinematic, lonely, reflective, and healing, with strong emotional metaphor. Use clear panel borders and clean sequencing. Do not make it realistic or 3D. Keep the illustration flat, graphic, and expressive like the reference images.\n\nCHARACTER CONSTRAINTS — apply to all frames:\nThe main character is a lonely golden masked humanoid in the same style as the reference images. He must remain visually consistent in all frames: golden body, black mask, white eyes, dark shorts or pants, one dark gray arm sleeve, strong simplified anatomy, expressive body language. He is the emotional focal point of the storyboard.\n\nLAYOUT + TEXT CONSTRAINTS — apply to all frames:\nCreate a vertical 9:16 cinematic storyboard collage with 4 separate frames stacked vertically.\nEach frame must have a clear visible label at the top-left corner in simple white handwritten text:\n“FRAME 01 — 10s–12.5s”\n“FRAME 02 — 12.5s–15s”\n“FRAME 03 — 15s–17.5s”\n“FRAME 04 — 17.5s–20s”\n\nAdd a small Vietnamese subtitle under each frame, clean and readable:\nFRAME 01: “Có thể bạn đang mắc sai lầm.”\nFRAME 02: “Sai lầm đầu tiên: ngẩng đầu lên.”\nFRAME 03: “Điều này gây căng cơ cổ.”\nFRAME 04: “Và làm lệch trục cơ thể.”\n\nFRAME CONTENT:\nFRAME 01 — 10s–12.5s:\nAthlete pauses during workout, breathing heavily while looking confused. Dark gym environment, cinematic overhead lighting, educational fitness atmosphere.\n\nFRAME 02 — 12.5s–15s:\nClose-up side profile of athlete doing push-up while lifting head too high. Neck bent unnaturally upward. Spine alignment visibly incorrect.\n\nFRAME 03 — 15s–17.5s:\nDetailed close-up of neck muscles under tension during incorrect push-up posture. Subtle red pain indicators around neck area, cinematic anatomy emphasis.\n\nFRAME 04 — 17.5s–20s:\nWide shot showing body misalignment caused by lifting head too high. Spine curve highlighted subtly with glowing guideline overlay. Realistic fitness documentary style.\n\nFINAL LOOK:\nDark cinematic gym storyboard with educational anatomy focus, realistic athletic movement, dramatic lighting, modern sports science aesthetic, ultra detailed fitness instructional visuals.",
