          "prompt": "Create a 10-second ultra-realistic vertical 9:16 cinematic automotive lifestyle video.\n\nUse the uploaded 4 reference images in this exact order:\n\nIMAGE 1 = FRONT/SIDE DRIVER IDENTITY + OUTFIT REFERENCE\nUse for the male driver’s appearance, hairstyle, white face mask, green-gray outfit, seated posture, and white Mercedes luxury interior mood.\n\nIMAGE 2 = FIRST-PERSON DRIVER POV REFERENCE\nUse for driver-eye-level view, both hands on the white Mercedes steering wheel, dashboard, center screen, and road ahead.\n\nIMAGE 3 = OVER-THE-SHOULDER DRIVING REFERENCE\nUse for behind-left-shoulder composition, side/back driver view, natural driving posture, and road visible through the windshield.\n\nIMAGE 4 = HIGH FRONT-PASSENGER / WINDSHIELD ANGLE REFERENCE\nUse for high diagonal interior angle, masked face, seatbelt, upper body, white cabin, sunroof, and front cabin spaciousness.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\n* Do not confuse the order of the 4 reference images.\n* Do not merge the images into one still.\n* Do not create a 4-panel storyboard.\n* Do not show multiple frames at once.\n* Create one continuous 10-second video using the 4 images as camera-angle and action references.\n* Keep the same driver, same outfit, same white mask, same car interior, same left-hand-drive layout, and same Ho Chi Minh City environment throughout.\n\nMAIN CONCEPT:\nA fashionable male driver drives a Mercedes-Maybach 2025 through Ho Chi Minh City, District 1, during daylight. The mood is premium, calm, cinematic, confident, and effortless luxury driving.\n\nDRIVER:\n\n* Male driver wearing a realistic white face mask.\n* Same green-gray outfit from the reference images.\n* Same hairstyle, eyes, eyebrows, upper-face identity, skin tone, and overall appearance throughout.\n* Calm, confident, stylish, focused, and composed.\n* No talking, phone use, dancing, waving, or exaggerated gestures.\n\nCAR INTERIOR:\n\n* Mercedes-Maybach 2025.\n* LEFT-HAND-DRIVE vehicle.\n* Driver seated on the LEFT side.\n* White Mercedes steering wheel on the LEFT side, directly in front of the driver.\n* Mercedes logo clearly visible at the center of the steering wheel whenever visible.\n* All-white luxury interior: white leather dashboard, white diamond-quilted seats, modern digital displays, large vertical center screen, panoramic sunroof.\n* Bright, spacious, premium cabin atmosphere.\n\nLEFT-HAND-DRIVE LOCK:\n\n* Do not create a right-hand-drive car.\n* Do not place the steering wheel on the right side.\n* Do not place the driver on the right side.\n* Do not mirror or flip the interior.\n* The driver must always remain seated on the LEFT side.\n* The white Mercedes steering wheel must always remain on the LEFT side.\n\nLOCATION:\nHo Chi Minh City, District 1. Outside the windows and windshield: modern Vietnamese urban street, tall buildings, mid-rise buildings, realistic traffic flow, cars, motorbikes, tropical daylight, upscale central-city atmosphere. No European streets, no American highway, no empty futuristic city, no foreign-looking environment.\n\nSTYLE:\nUltra-realistic, cinematic, professional automotive lifestyle video. Smooth natural cuts, realistic daylight, subtle motion blur outside windows. Interior, driver, mask, outfit, hands, steering wheel, dashboard, and Mercedes logo remain sharp. No CGI, no AI artifacts, no distorted hands, no warped steering wheel, no face or outfit changing between shots.\n\nTIMELINE:\n\n0.0s – 2.5s — HIGH INTERIOR ANGLE, LIKE IMAGE 4\nCamera:\n\n* High diagonal interior angle from upper windshield / front passenger-side area, looking down toward the driver.\n* Show masked face, eyes, upper body, seatbelt, white steering wheel, white cabin, panoramic sunroof, and city street outside.\n\nAction:\n\n* Driver looks calmly forward through the windshield.\n* Both hands stay near the steering wheel.\n* He makes a very slight natural head movement as the car moves.\n* Seatbelt lies diagonally across his chest with realistic tension over the outfit.\n* Sunlight passes through the panoramic sunroof and windshield.\n* White mask fully covers nose and mouth.\n* Mercedes logo remains visible on the white steering wheel.\n* No exterior shot, no right-hand-drive layout.\n\n2.5s – 5.0s — FIRST-PERSON DRIVER POV, LIKE IMAGE 2\nCamera:\n\n* Driver-eye-level POV from the LEFT side of the cabin.\n* Looking forward through the windshield.\n* White Mercedes steering wheel fills the foreground.\n* Both hands and green-gray sleeves are visible.\n* Dashboard, digital display, center screen, A-pillars, and city road ahead are visible.\n\nAction:\n\n* Driver holds the wheel naturally with both hands.\n* Hands make a very subtle steering correction, no aggressive movement.\n* Car continues moving forward smoothly.\n* Motorbikes and cars ahead move naturally with slight motion blur.\n* Do not show the driver’s face in this POV shot.\n* Only hands, forearms, sleeves, steering wheel, dashboard, and road ahead are visible.\n* Mercedes logo must be centered and clear.\n\n5.0s – 7.5s — OVER-THE-SHOULDER SHOT, LIKE IMAGE 3\nCamera:\n\n* Behind-left-shoulder angle.\n* Camera is slightly behind and to the left of the driver’s shoulder.\n* Looking forward over the shoulder toward the windshield and road.\n* Show back/side head edge, shoulder, sleeve, left hand, white steering wheel, dashboard, and road ahead.\n\nAction:\n\n* Driver keeps his gaze forward.\n* One hand adjusts slightly on the steering wheel.\n* Shoulder moves subtly with the car motion.\n* A small side edge of the white mask may be visible near the cheek or ear loop.\n* Do not show a full frontal face.\n* Do not turn this into a rear-seat wide shot.\n* Keep the white cabin, dashboard, and road movement consistent.\n\n7.5s – 10.0s — FRONT/SIDE HERO ANGLE, LIKE IMAGE 1\nCamera:\n\n* Front/side interior angle.\n* Show the driver from the front-side inside the cabin.\n* Visible: white mask, eyes, hairstyle, upper body, green-gray outfit, white steering wheel, white seat, sunroof, and city buildings outside.\n* The angle feels close, premium, and cinematic.\n\nAction:\n\n* Driver briefly glances slightly toward the camera with calm confident eyes, then returns gaze to the road.\n* One hand remains on the steering wheel.\n* Posture stays relaxed and stylish.\n* Car continues driving smoothly through the city.\n* No forced smile, no exaggerated acting.\n* End with a composed luxury driving moment.\n\nCONSISTENCY:\n\n* Same white mask in every visible face shot.\n* Mask fully covers nose and mouth; straps sit naturally around ears.\n* Same driver identity, hairstyle, eyes, eyebrows, and upper-face proportions.\n* Same green-gray outfit throughout.\n* Preserve outfit color blocking, sleeve stripes, collar, zipper, logo placement if visible, fabric texture, and sporty jacket shape.\n* Fabric folds and seatbelt pressure look natural.\n\nCAMERA / EDITING RULES:\n\n* Use the 4 reference images as sequential camera-angle references.\n* Clean cinematic cuts are allowed.\n* Do not blend two camera angles together.\n* No sudden jumpy camera, spinning camera, drone shot, exterior car shot, impossible camera movement, duplicated drivers, split screen, collage, storyboard grid, text, captions, added logos, or watermark.\n\nSTRICT NEGATIVE RULES:\n\n* No right-hand-drive layout.\n* No steering wheel on the right side.\n* No driver sitting on the right side.\n* No mirrored or flipped cabin.\n* No black steering wheel.\n* No missing Mercedes logo.\n* No unmasked driver.\n* No changed face or outfit between shots.\n* No deformed hands, extra fingers, floating hands, warped steering wheel, distorted dashboard.\n* No dashboard blocking the main view.\n* No unrealistic city environment.\n* No exterior-only shot.\n* No AI-looking face, plastic skin, CGI look, cartoon, illustration, or digital painting.\n\nOUTPUT:\n\n* Duration: 10 seconds.\n* Aspect ratio: 9:16 vertical.\n* Ultra-realistic.\n* High-resolution.\n* Cinematic automotive lifestyle video.\n* One continuous driving sequence using the 4 uploaded images as ordered visual references.",
