          "prompt": "GLOBAL CHARACTER REFERENCE LOCK\n\nUse the supplied Tom and Jerry streetwear image as the strict identity, character-design, clothing and material reference only.\n\nCharacter A is Tom, the tall anthropomorphic grey-blue cat.\n\nPreserve Tom exactly:\ngrey-blue detailed fur, white muzzle and chest, large pointed ears with pink inner ears, yellow eyes, black sunglasses, royal-blue hoodie, gold chain necklace, distressed dark-grey jeans, blue-grey-white high-top sneakers, tall slim anthropomorphic cartoon proportions.\n\nCharacter B is Jerry, the small anthropomorphic brown mouse.\n\nPreserve Jerry exactly:\nwarm brown detailed fur, large round ears with pink inner ears, round sunglasses, black cap with the word “BOSS”, black hoodie, gold chain necklace, white sneakers, small rounded anthropomorphic cartoon proportions.\n\nMaintain the exact size relationship:\nTom is much taller and larger than Jerry.\n\nDo not turn either character into a human.\nDo not change their species, faces, fur colors, body proportions, clothing, shoes, jewelry or eyewear.\nDo not copy the outdoor street, graffiti, sunset or sports car from the original image.\nThe new environment must be an underground parking garage.\n\nConsistent cinematic realistic 3D CG character rendering, detailed realistic fur, physically based fabric materials, subtle cinematic film grain, Unreal Engine 5 visual quality.\n\nUse GLOBAL CHARACTER REFERENCE LOCK.\n9:16 cinematic portrait.\nThe camera is positioned directly behind Tom at upper-body height inside the same underground parking garage. Show only the back of Tom’s head, pointed ears, shoulders, royal-blue hoodie and part of his upper back.\n\nTom faces away from the camera toward the empty parking garage. His posture is still, controlled and confident. Preserve the exact hoodie design, fabric texture, body proportions, ear shape and grey-blue fur from the character reference.\n\nThe parking space directly in front of Tom is empty. No character is standing behind or beside him. Jerry must not be visible anywhere in the frame.\n\nEnvironment continuity:\nsame concrete ceiling, same cold-white fluorescent light array, same columns, same dark parking bays, same cool grey-blue industrial color palette and same high-contrast lighting as image 1.\n\nCamera:\ndirect rear view, centered symmetrical composition, medium close shot, approximately 50mm lens.\n\nDo not show Tom’s face.\nDo not show Jerry.\nNo humans.\nNo duplicated character.\nNo outdoor street.\nNo sunset.\nNo graffiti.\nNo text.",
