          "slug": "global_scene_lock",
          "slug_auto": false,
          "node_name": "Text",
          "node_type": "text",
          "provider": null,
          "prompt": "GLOBAL SCENE REFERENCE LOCK\n\nUse the provided reference image as the fixed scene, composition, environment and camera reference.\n\nAutomatically analyze and preserve:\n\nthe exact location shown in the reference image\nroad, pavement, bridge structure, walls, pillars, buildings, fences, trees and surrounding objects\ncamera position, camera height, camera angle, framing and perspective\nspatial proportions and distances between all permanent elements\nthe original ground surface and architectural details\n\nThe location may be a street corner, an area beneath a bridge, an alley, a sidewalk, an empty lot or another public space. Adapt naturally to the specific reference image.\n\nOnly change:\n\nthe amount and position of removable trash\nthe presence, positions and cleaning actions of sanitation workers\ntemporary cleaning equipment, trash bags, carts, brooms, shovels and waste containers\n\nDo not redesign or replace the location.\nDo not change the camera viewpoint between storyboard images.\nDo not add new buildings, roads, vehicles or permanent structures.\nDo not remove objects that are part of the original location.\nMaintain strong visual continuity across all three images.",
