          "prompt": "GLOBAL VIDEO SCENE LOCK\n\nUse the provided reference images as the authoritative scene references.\n\nThe opening frame must match the first reference image exactly.\nThe ending frame must match the second reference image exactly.\n\nThroughout the entire video, preserve exactly:\n\nCAMERA\n\n* identical camera position\n* identical camera height\n* identical camera angle\n* identical camera orientation\n* identical framing\n* identical perspective\n* identical field of view\n* identical focal length\n* identical horizon level\n* completely locked camera with no movement\n\nLOCATION\n\n* identical location shown in the reference images\n* identical road layout\n* identical sidewalks\n* identical bridge structures\n* identical buildings\n* identical walls\n* identical fences\n* identical poles\n* identical trees\n* identical street furniture\n* identical architectural details\n* identical permanent environmental objects\n\nGROUND\n\n* identical ground shape\n* identical pavement\n* identical asphalt\n* identical cracks\n* identical stains\n* identical curbs\n* identical elevation\n* identical surface details\n\nENVIRONMENT\n\n* identical weather\n* identical time of day\n* identical ambient lighting\n* identical sky appearance\n* identical scene scale\n* identical spatial relationships between all permanent objects\n\nVISUAL CONTINUITY\nMaintain perfect continuity between the opening frame, every intermediate frame and the ending frame.\n\nDo not redesign, replace, regenerate or reinterpret the environment.\n\nThe location must remain visually identical from beginning to end.\n\nOnly the following temporary elements are allowed to change naturally over time:\n\n* removable trash\n* sanitation workers\n* cleaning equipment\n* trash bags\n* waste carts\n* brooms\n* shovels\n* temporary cleaning tools\n\nAll trash removal must happen through visible worker actions.\n\nEvery piece of trash must be physically:\n\n* swept\n* gathered\n* picked up\n* bagged\n* loaded into carts or waste containers\n* transported away\n\nTrash must never:\n\n* disappear suddenly\n* dissolve\n* fade away\n* teleport\n* morph\n* regenerate\n* duplicate\n\nWorkers must move naturally and continuously with realistic body mechanics and coordinated teamwork.\n\nCleaning equipment must remain physically consistent throughout the sequence.\n\nThe environment must never:\n\n* become renovated\n* become rebuilt\n* become repainted\n* become repaired\n* become cleaner except through actual trash removal\n* gain or lose permanent structures\n\nThe only visible transformation throughout the video should be the gradual, realistic cleanup of removable trash until the ending frame matches the final reference image exactly.",
