          "node_type": "prompt",
          "provider": null,
          "prompt": "VIDEO 1 — CONTINUOUS CLEANUP TIMELAPSE FROM IMAGE 1 TO IMAGE 2\n\nREFERENCE USAGE\n\nUse Image 1 as the exact first frame and primary scene reference.\n\nUse Image 2 only as the required cleanup-progress target for the final frame.\n\nThe video must begin with the scene matching Image 1 and gradually evolve until the final frame matches Image 2.\n\nTIMELAPSE MOTION FORMAT\n\nCreate one uninterrupted, single-shot, fixed-camera timelapse.\n\nThe video must look like one long continuous cleaning process recorded by a stationary camera and played back at high speed.\n\nAll workers must move rapidly, fluidly and continuously throughout the same uninterrupted timeline.\n\nTheir movements should appear as natural accelerated human motion, with subtle fast-motion trails or temporal motion blur where appropriate.\n\nDo not create a montage.\n\nDo not divide the process into separate shots, mini-scenes, chapters, stages or edited clips.\n\nDo not use:\n\n* jump cuts\n* hidden cuts\n* match cuts\n* time jumps\n* scene transitions\n* dissolves\n* fades\n* black frames\n* camera-angle changes\n* close-up inserts\n* repeated action loops\n* stop-motion movement\n* sudden character repositioning\n\nCONTINUOUS ACTION\n\nAt the beginning, all trash visible in Image 1 remains in place.\n\nThe sanitation workers immediately begin moving quickly and continuously around the scene.\n\nThey perform overlapping cleaning actions within the same fixed wide shot:\n\n* workers walk rapidly between littered areas\n* workers continuously sweep loose waste across the ground\n* waste gradually gathers into increasingly organized piles\n* workers bend down, pick up litter and place it into bags\n* partially filled bags progressively become fuller\n* filled bags are carried continuously toward one temporary collection point\n* workers return immediately to continue cleaning\n* cleaning tools remain in active use throughout the process\n\nThe workers must not pause to pose or remain static for long periods.\n\nSeveral workers may perform different actions simultaneously, creating constant visible activity across the frame.\n\nPROGRESSIVE TRASH REDUCTION\n\nTrash must reduce gradually and continuously throughout the entire video.\n\nThe transformation must be visible frame by frame:\n\n* individual pieces are swept toward piles\n* piles gradually become denser\n* workers physically collect the piles\n* bags gradually fill\n* cleaned ground is progressively revealed behind the moving workers\n\nTrash must never disappear between frames without visible physical handling.\n\nDo not replace the dirty scene with a cleaner scene through an edit.\n\nDo not instantly switch from 100% trash to 50% trash.\n\nThe cleanup boundary must move naturally across the location as workers complete one small area and immediately continue into the next.\n\nENDING CONTINUITY\n\nDuring the final portion, approximately 50% of the original trash has been physically removed.\n\nOne section is visibly clean while the remaining section still contains the same recognizable trash clusters required for Video 2.\n\nEnd while the workers are still actively moving and cleaning.\n\nThe final movement must remain unfinished so Video 2 can continue directly without a pause.\n\nThe final frame must match Image 2 as closely as possible.\n\nThe entire result must feel like a single continuous high-speed recording, not several short videos edited together.",
